# p t_ranspose A permutes the axes (B17): p lists each axis of A once,
# and axis i of A becomes axis p[i] of the result (APL's dyadic
# transpose, without diagonals). The reversed identity is o_\, the
# identity leaves A as it is.
== SOURCE
m := 2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6
a := 2 3 4 r_eshape r_ange 24
s_hape 2 1 3 t_ranspose a
s_hape 3 1 2 t_ranspose a
1 s_elect 3 1 2 t_ranspose a
(2 1 t_ranspose m) m_atch o_\ m
(3 2 1 t_ranspose a) m_atch o_\ a
(1 2 3 t_ranspose a) m_atch a
1 t_ranspose 1 2 3
== RESULT
3 2 4
3 4 2
1 13
2 14
3 15
4 16
1
1
1
1 2 3
